{"id": "sungrow-2026-09-14-007", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["sungrow"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["increase", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Sungrow raises inverter, storage prices by up to 15%", "content": "<p>Sungrow will raise prices for solar inverters and energy storage products by 5% to 15% from Sept. 20, citing rising raw material and component costs. The move, its second price increase this year, reflects broader cost pressures across China’s inverter and storage supply chains.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/14/sungrow-raises-inverter-storage-prices-by-up-to-15/\">Sungrow raises inverter, storage prices by up to 15%</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-m", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/14/sungrow-raises-inverter-storage-prices-by-up-to-15/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-14-008", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Researchers find perovskite solar functions 10 meters below sea surface", "content": "<p>Research from China deployed lead halide perovskites 10 meters below the surface of the South China Sea. The cells generated 324 mWh, enough to charge lithium-ion batteries, when submerged for two hours.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/14/researchers-find-perovskite-solar-functions-10-meters-below-sea-surface/\">Researchers find perovskite solar functions 10 meters below sea surface</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/14/researchers-find-perovskite-solar-functions-10-meters-below-sea-surface/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-14-009", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Australia to introduce technical code for consumer energy resources", "content": "<p>Australia's new regulatory framework for solar inverters, batteries and other consumer energy resources will require suppliers to register products and prove compliance with a technical code. It also introduces national-level accreditation for installers.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/14/australia-to-introduce-technical-code-for-consumer-energy-resources/\">Australia to introduce technical code for consumer energy resources</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/14/australia-to-introduce-technical-code-for-consumer-energy-resources/", "type": "rss"}]}
